{
  "id": "COMPOUND:33087 - PROTEIN:5836",
  "verbalization": "The dimethyl (1S,9R,15S,16S,17S,18R,21R)-15,17,18-trihydroxy-2,12-diazahexacyclo[14.2.2.19,12.01,9.03,8.016,21]henicosa-3,5,7-triene-2,18-dicarboxylate appears to be a target of multiple entities that ultimately interact with HUVEC, a human vascular endothelial cell line. This compound is a target of three distinct molecules: WS-5995 B, 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, and Oleamide. These molecules are all known to interact with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, a protein involved in epigenetic regulation. The presence of multiple targets that share a common mechanism of action—likely involving the modulation of demethylase activity—suggests a potential role for this compound in influencing HUVEC function. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and HUVEC, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mechanism of action.",
